Supervised learning is a scenario in which the learner uses labeled training data, where the training examples contain significant information (such as labels) that is missing in the unseen test examples. The goal is to learn a classifier that will predict the labels of future examples as accurately as possible. A supervised learner can also estimate the success or risk of its hypotheses using the labeled training data by computing the empirical loss.

